WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:03.042
- That is a bad rumor, but the
biggest thing—it’s a rumor

00:00:03.042 --> 00:00:04.792
-Ugh! Grrr!

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:07.417
I looked like a wimp last week

00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:09.792
so I'm gonna grind
my teeth this week!

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:11.542
-You know,
I once beat up Ray Lewis

00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:13.542
-What? Yeah, I mean—
-That’s another story I could
tell

00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:17.542
♪♪

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:18.792
-What is up?

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:20.417
And welcome back
to "Simms &amp; Lefkoe"

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:21.667
Headed into Week 4

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.167
Week 3 is in the books!

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.667
And Monday night, I thought,
"Oh, no

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.667
The end of Ryan Fitzpatrick
has come”

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.625
Second half,
almost wins the game

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.917
Where are you on
the Ryan Fitzpatrick

00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:33.625
“It's over/He’s
still going" meter?

00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:36.417
-I'm over talking about it
on a weekly basis already

00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:38.417
I know that.
Like, we're, like, every week

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:39.750
Hey, he had a rough first half

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.417
against a desperate
Steeler team

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.625
but battled back
and made some big-time plays

00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:45.750
-Still his team?
-Definitely still his team

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.125
What's more annoying about the
“Monday Night Football” game is

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:50.750
that game should have been over
about a quarter before it was

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.292
but we are not allowed
to blow in the ear

00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:54.917
of quarterbacks anymore,
and those are penalties

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:56.667
-But you're a quarterback,
Chris Simms!

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.792
-I don't care. I'm old-school,
and they need to hit them.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.792
Hit them hard
-I don't want anyone to hit

00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:03.542
Ryan Fitzpatrick
after I saw him doing this

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.292
-Pure, unadulterated joy

00:01:06.292 --> 00:01:08.250
This is after
the Mike Evans touchdown

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.417
Now, Fitzpatrick, he did get
sacked a few times last night

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:13.167
We got to see his sack face

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.042
And we had everyone reach out,
and, boy

00:01:15.042 --> 00:01:16.625
did we get a lot of yours
-Right

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:19.625
-Of their quarterbacks getting
sacked in Week 3

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.000
And we wanna take people into
the minds of the quarterbacks

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.708
as they get sacked,
so you go first

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:26.208
-Oh, Eli!

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:28.208
"Ugh! Grrr!

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:30.458
I looked like a wimp last week

00:01:30.458 --> 00:01:33.458
so I'm gonna grind my teeth
this week!

00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:37.000
I can take a shot
from the gut from J.J. Watt!

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Ahhh, tough Eli memes this week!

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.833
Grrr!"

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.833
-Alex Smith
-"Um, Cali, bro!

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:48.375
Look at how my hand's ridin' the
wave of this football, man

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:51.000
Super loose, super chill,
super cool"

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Do your favorite
quarterback here

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.000
-Oh, my favorite quarterback.
"Hi, I'm Aaron Rodgers

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
So, uh, I’ve been carrying this team
for 10 years

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Let me just carry
the Redskins along with me

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.500
I hope this guy throws me down
like a rag doll

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.917
and then they won't call it

00:02:03.917 --> 00:02:05.500
but they'll call it on my guy
later on, Clay Matthews

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.500
when he makes
a perfect form tackle”

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.250
-All right, I got Andrew Luck

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.750
"Dearest Rebecca,
I ask you to remember me

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.375
not for this sack,
but for my career as a whole

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:21.375
Signing off—
Your captain, Andrew Luck"

00:02:21.375 --> 00:02:23.250
Oh, look who it is, Simms

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.875
-Oh, look who it is

00:02:24.875 --> 00:02:26.958
-Getting a shot to Peppers
right in the old gut

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:30.125
-"Oh, oh, please, Julius,
don't hit me in the spleen!

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:32.250
It's already losing blood
at this point

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.500
Hit me a little lower
than the spleen

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.875
It won't hurt

00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:38.250
Oh, I'm still tough
and losing blood

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.250
and dying on the field,
but I'm playing!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:43.125
Now, I’m—Gosh,
I might have to retire early

00:02:43.125 --> 00:02:45.708
and go work with some idiot
named Lefkoe at one point"

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:47.625
-Wait, so you're telling me

00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:50.750
that the game that we chose
for your sack face…

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.125
-I am truly—
-…that was the spleen game?

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:54.000
And that's after
you lost your spleen?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.958
-Well, I didn’t—
-Well, busted your spleen
-I mean, it's being destructed

00:02:56.958 --> 00:02:58.500
as we were watching it
right there

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.000
It's bleeding internally

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.750
But it just shows you
how tough I am

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.583
Look, losing blood—I
don't even make a wimpy face.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:07.250
I'm just like, “Grrr! Losing
blood, dying—doesn't matter!"

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.500
-See, that's why you're OK
with the roughing the passer

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.500
You're able to look
at your stuff

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.500
you're a true self-scout,
and I'm really proud of you

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.000
-Thank you for being proud

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.875
-But I think we need to do
some self-scouting
-OK

00:03:16.875 --> 00:03:18.208
-I want some more analysis
-Sure

00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:20.125
-It's what separates us
as analysts

00:03:20.125 --> 00:03:22.333
We're OK admitting
when we're wrong

00:03:22.333 --> 00:03:23.625
Jared Goff
-Yeah

00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:25.625
-You were questioning
his abilities

00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:27.708
questioning his talent

00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:29.375
Look, even our fans upset with
you

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.125
"Keep the Rams
out of your mouth

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:34.125
Gurley was a one-hit wonder.
STFU," all that stuff.

00:03:34.125 --> 00:03:36.000
But a lot of Rams fans
have come at you

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.625
and your criticism of Goff

00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:39.083
-OK
-Self-scout yourself

00:03:39.083 --> 00:03:40.583
-Yeah, well, I mean, Goff

00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:42.375
I think what I said early on
is what he was

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.083
The fact that I would—

00:03:44.083 --> 00:03:45.958
Do I wanna say he's a system
quarterback early on?

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.583
Hey, he was the No. 1 pick
of the draft

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.958
and he had to be massaged a
little bit

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.375
his first year or two, OK?

00:03:51.375 --> 00:03:53.708
-How about now, though?
-But right now?

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:55.625
Yes, I mean,
we're seeing a new Jared Goff

00:03:55.625 --> 00:03:58.208
We're seeing a guy
that is not actually managing

00:03:58.208 --> 00:04:01.000
the offense or McVay’s making
things so easy for him

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.875
What I've seen in the first
three games from Jared Goff is

00:04:03.875 --> 00:04:06.750
actually a guy that I'm going,
"Wow, gettin’ outta the pocket

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.375
makin’ big-time throws
on the run

00:04:08.375 --> 00:04:11.250
Wow, throwin’ 101 mph
fastballs and painting

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.250
the corner into a tight window
to a receiver," or

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:17.083
“Wow, a bomb throw down the
field,
right on the money"

00:04:17.083 --> 00:04:19.375
So, those are things
that I didn't see

00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:21.750
I thought the offense
and the talent around him

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.750
early on was more carrying him
than the other way around

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.958
but we're seeing a guy
that's coming into his own

00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:30.500
right in front of us,
and I got no problem with that

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.125
I'm not gonna STFU,
but FU to Brandon McIntosh
-[Laughing]

00:04:34.125 --> 00:04:36.125
-I hear that you have
a self-scout for me

00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:38.750
-[Laughing]
This is gonna be more fun

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.958
Have you seen
Lefkoe's Locks lately?

00:04:40.958 --> 00:04:42.958
Let's self-scout that!

00:04:42.958 --> 00:04:44.958
-Why?
-Cuz they're horrible!

00:04:44.958 --> 00:04:47.083
-What's so wrong with them?
-You're 0-8!

00:04:47.083 --> 00:04:48.583
-So, the last two weeks,
I'm 0-8

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:50.500
It's my job to pick games
-Right

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.875
-It's their job to decide
what to do with my picks

00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:56.208
-Ohhh
-If they would've bet against me

00:04:56.208 --> 00:04:57.958
all four games in a $100 parlay,
you know how much money

00:04:57.958 --> 00:04:59.000
they'd have?
-Right

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.500
-Nearly $1,500

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.875
If they did it for two weeks

00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:02.875
you know how much money
they'd have?

00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:04.458
Nearly $25,000

00:05:04.458 --> 00:05:05.750
-Man, I’m still thinking about
0-8.
I can't even—

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.208
-Yeah, well, guess what?

00:05:07.208 --> 00:05:09.750
Michelangelo didn't paint
the Sistine Chapel

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.125
cuz he thought
he was more of a sculptor

00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:13.125
-Huh
-I thought I was
a winner-picker

00:05:13.125 --> 00:05:16.208
I'm not.
I'm a Lefkoe Loser Locker, OK?

00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:19.125
So use my information correctly

00:05:19.125 --> 00:05:20.958
and maybe you would've made
some money

00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:23.000
This is not a "me" issue,
it's a "them" issue, Simms

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.250
-Oh, I gotcha

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.708
You're such
a diva wide receiver
-Yes

00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:27.708
It's disgusting.
“He's open every play, Coach.

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:30.125
Throw it to him.
It's never his fault.”

00:05:30.125 --> 00:05:32.208
-I have a story from another
diva wide receiver

00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:34.125
Little Chad Johnson
-Oooh

00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:36.958
-Where he claims that
he almost beat up Ray Lewis

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:38.250
Almost

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.625
-Yeah, right
-Almost

00:05:39.625 --> 00:05:41.125
-Good luck, Chad

00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:42.833
-You know,
I almost beat up Ray Lewis

00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:44.750
-What? Yeah, I mean—
-Another story I could tell

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.208
-I like the way you say "almost"

00:05:46.208 --> 00:05:48.708
-"Almost" is the key phrase
-You “almost" beat nobody

00:05:48.708 --> 00:05:51.000
-Because, listen, Ray and I are
very good friends

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.625
similar to how T.O. and I are

00:05:52.625 --> 00:05:55.375
So, we're playing the Ravens.
We're in Baltimore.

00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:57.333
Ray and I talked
before the game

00:05:57.333 --> 00:05:59.500
We did our ritual
that we always do

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.458
We always met at the 50,
and we’d say a short prayer

00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:02.750
In the game, at some point

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.750
there was a slant
that was thrown too high

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:08.625
He hit me, and the safety hit me
at the same time in a sandwich

00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:10.458
-Yeah
-My helmet went flying
-Right

00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:13.875
-And I jumped up, and I ran
at Ray like we was gonna fight

00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:15.708
Obviously, I wasn’t gonna hit
him during the game

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.333
cuz I didn't wanna
get thrown out

00:06:17.333 --> 00:06:18.583
-Right
-But where could I catch Ray?

00:06:18.583 --> 00:06:19.625
In the locker room

00:06:19.625 --> 00:06:21.000
-After the game
-After the game

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.708
-What?
-So, what do I do?

00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:25.375
I put on my tight jeans
cuz, you know, all my clothes
are tight

00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:27.125
-Right
-Tie up my shoes real tight

00:06:27.125 --> 00:06:28.875
and I go towards
the Ravens locker room

00:06:28.875 --> 00:06:31.750
I ask Ed [Reed], "Where's Ray?"
And I just wanna talk.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.000
Man, Ray had went out
the back door

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.125
and he already headin’
to the car

00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:37.958
So I go out to the parking lot

00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:40.750
and he pullin’ off,
and I'm runnin’ after Ray's car

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.625
-You got a shirt on
now and everything?

00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:44.583
-No shirt.
I'm runnin’ after Ray’s car.

00:06:44.583 --> 00:06:46.833
I'm like, "Yo!"
-Yeah

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:48.708
-And I know he can see me
in the rearview mirror

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:51.375
cuz at that time, you know,
I had a little size on me
-[Laughing]

00:06:51.375 --> 00:06:54.208
-I can barely see him now
-I don't think Ray
really wanted that beef

00:06:54.208 --> 00:06:56.875
You know, cuz I'm a boxer.
I box.

00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:58.458
-Yeah
-You know?

00:06:58.458 --> 00:07:00.375
And I think he understood
and knows about my hands

00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:02.083
-[Laughing]
-And, therefore, he didn't wanna

00:07:02.083 --> 00:07:04.750
get shown up, and
Ed Reed really saved Ray

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.000
by holding me up
-Giving a little more time
to get away

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.625
-To get to his car.
That's what happened.

00:07:08.625 --> 00:07:10.625
-Ray, you see how close you were
to gettin’ your ass beat

00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:11.875
by Ochocinco?

00:07:11.875 --> 00:07:13.875
-Almost

00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:15.833
-Yeah, Chad, almost

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.833
All right, we have three-time
Pro Bowler DeMarco Murray

00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:19.625
in the house

00:07:19.625 --> 00:07:21.958
DeMarco, we want to play a game
that we call "Depth Chart"

00:07:21.958 --> 00:07:23.750
I'm gonna give you
three names and a scenario

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.833
and you have to tell me
which one you're going to start

00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:29.000
which one is the backup and
which one is in street clothes

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.375
-OK
-So the first scenario is this

00:07:31.375 --> 00:07:33.750
A baby is falling
out of a window

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:38.125
Which of these running backs do
you trust the most to catch it?

00:07:38.125 --> 00:07:40.333
Start, backup, healthy scratch

00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:44.958
Darren Sproles, David Johnson,
Le'Veon Bell

00:07:44.958 --> 00:07:46.750
-Hopefully it's not
my baby, but, uh…

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.000
[Laughing]

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.500
I would say Sproles

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.458
-OK
-Because he's a little softer

00:07:51.458 --> 00:07:53.500
he's a smaller guy,
and he won't hurt the baby

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.125
when he catches the baby

00:07:55.125 --> 00:07:56.500
-I agree with that.
It's gonna be a soft landing.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.208
-It's gonna be a soft landing.

00:07:58.208 --> 00:08:00.333
I would say David Johnson
is my backup

00:08:00.333 --> 00:08:02.417
-Yeah, I don't trust
Le'Veon Bell catching my baby

00:08:02.417 --> 00:08:04.208
Not at this point
-Le'Veon Bell, he may be
rapping or doing something

00:08:04.208 --> 00:08:07.083
He may be—his
mind may be elsewhere

00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:08.583
and let the baby fall
and splat

00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:10.208
-He might be like,
“I’ll catch this baby if I get a
new contract”

00:08:10.208 --> 00:08:13.000
-He might be like, “Hold on,
hold on,
my agent's calling. Hold on."

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.500
-He may be elsewhere mentally.
Mentally, he may be elsewhere.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:17.125
-All right.
Your Uber didn't show up.

00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:19.625
You need someone reliable
to pick you up

00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:21.667
Who do you call?

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:25.875
Jason Witten, Delanie Walker,
Zach Ertz

00:08:25.875 --> 00:08:27.667
-Hmmm, that's a good choice
there

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:29.708
-Tight ends are reliable
-That’s tough
-They are reliable

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:31.708
I mean, I gotta go
with my man Witt

00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:33.583
I mean, Witt is always on time.
He's never late.

00:08:33.583 --> 00:08:34.958
-Yes
-Every time he's told me

00:08:34.958 --> 00:08:37.208
he'll be somewhere, he's there

00:08:37.208 --> 00:08:38.958
I would say Zach Ertz…

00:08:38.958 --> 00:08:40.708
Delanie's a
little different now

00:08:40.708 --> 00:08:42.417
Delanie, you know,
Delanie may be

00:08:42.417 --> 00:08:44.917
“Yeah, you know, I
gotta talk to this girl"

00:08:44.917 --> 00:08:46.167
He has this voice
-[Laughing]

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:48.042
-If you know Delanie,
he has this voice

00:08:48.042 --> 00:08:49.708
Like, "Yeah, man,
I got caught up"

00:08:49.708 --> 00:08:51.083
You know, he has this voice

00:08:51.083 --> 00:08:52.333
I can’t, I can't imitate
-He might be doing something

00:08:52.333 --> 00:08:53.583
-He may be doing something else

00:08:53.583 --> 00:08:55.208
-He's gonna B.S. you
and be late

00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:56.750
-He's hilarious, yeah

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.125
So you got Witten as the start

00:08:58.125 --> 00:08:59.542
Ertz as the backup

00:08:59.542 --> 00:09:02.542
and then Delanie is
the street clothes

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:04.250
-Yeah
-And you know Witten

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.833
He's like Johnny Perfect
over there, right?

00:09:05.833 --> 00:09:07.583
-He might give me a lesson

00:09:07.583 --> 00:09:09.875
-Yeah, but it's always a lesson
that you can take, you know?

00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:12.083
